{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950999-2e-withstanding-merits","id":950999,"title":"[2E] Withstanding + Merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-15T02:34:47-07:00","id":950999,"title":"[2E] Withstanding + Merits","content":"Topic for talking about interaction between Withstanding mechanics with particular Merits.<br /> <br /> On last game session two my players were put under Mind 2 <i>Psychic Domination</i> spell. It says it resisted with Resolve. One PC is very high in Attribute ( it has Resolve 4 ) but also have <i>Indomitable</i> Merit ( <b>CoD</b> rulebook, page 45 ). Merits write up says about dice penalty to it's pool for 'monster' when activating power. <b>What to do if he is casting it on two targets ( two PCs ) and only one of them have </b><i><b>Indomitable?</b> </i>How to run Withstanding with that Merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T03:08:36-07:00","id":951012,"title":"","content":"It's a Merit that was written before the Withstand system. Since the effects of the Merit, even if not written precisely this way are +2 Resolve (either +2 dice when rolling Resolve to contest, or an addition -2 dice for the power if Resisted), I'd just say the Indomitable increases Resolve based Withstand against mental influence powers by 2. This also neatly resolves how to deal with a spell targeting multiple individuals, since you can compare each Withstand rating individually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T08:44:11-07:00","id":951745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950999-2e-withstanding-merits?p=951012#post951012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a Merit that was written before the Withstand system. Since the effects of the Merit, even if not written precisely this way are +2 Resolve (either +2 dice when rolling Resolve to contest, or an addition -2 dice for the power if Resisted), I'd just say the Indomitable increases Resolve based Withstand against mental influence powers by 2. This also neatly resolves how to deal with a spell targeting multiple individuals, since you can compare each Withstand rating individually.</div> </div> </div> </div>The effect is -2 to the roll if it isn't contested, which is how mage spells work. However, withstand is effectively 2 dice per point because of how increasing potency works. Because of this, I'd call indomitable a +1 withstand.<br /> <br /> Edit - For numbers comparison: average starting ventrue and mind mage vs average indomitable person. 2s for all relevant stats and the mage has a spell as a rote.<br /> <br /> 2 intelligence, 2 expression, 2 dominate (6) vs 2 resolve + 2 indomitable (4). Average rolls are 2 vs 1.3, vampire is likely to succeed.<br /> <br /> 2 mind, 2 rote mudra, 1 gnosis to best withstanding of 4 (resolve + indomitable). Required potency 5, primary factor raises it to 2. That's 3 more potency needed, or -6 dice. The mage is rolling a chance die, so success is unlikely.<br /> <br /> Even with it just being 1 withstand, that's 4 potency and a single regular die for the mage - not as good a shot as the vampire, but that makes sense because the vampire can just dominate while mind magic has other tricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11862,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","user":"Ifisa","date":". 08-16-2016, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:35:35-07:00","id":951869,"title":"","content":"Indomitable does nothing to Withstand ratings","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:39:32-07:00","id":951876,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, while I don't think I'd ever write it into a book, an Epic version of Indomitable that did add to Withstand Ratings kind of sounds rad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:16:44-07:00","id":951908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950999-2e-withstanding-merits?p=951869#post951869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indomitable does nothing to Withstand ratings</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Does any 'normal' Merit changes Withstand rating?<br /> 2. Should I offer player XP refund as she took this Merit <i>precisely</i> to be more resistant to mind control powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-16-2016, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:45:43-07:00","id":951932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950999-2e-withstanding-merits?p=951908#post951908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Does any 'normal' Merit changes Withstand rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall any.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Should I offer player XP refund as she took this Merit <i>precisely</i> to be more resistant to mind control powers? </div> </div> </div>Either that, or houserule it to grant +1 Resolve for Withstand purposes. It's not like anyone is going to chase you down and burn your books.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:54:44-07:00","id":951943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950999-2e-withstanding-merits?p=951908#post951908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Does any 'normal' Merit changes Withstand rating?<br /> 2. Should I offer player XP refund as she took this Merit <i>precisely</i> to be more resistant to mind control powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:56:59-07:00","id":951945,"title":"","content":"The Indomitable Merit does nothing to Withstand ratings.<br /> &quot;(...) Any time a supernatural creature uses a power to influence your character\u2019s thoughts or emotions, add two dice to the dice pool to contest it. If the roll is resisted, instead subtract two dice from the monster\u2019s dice pool.&quot;<br /> Withstand ratings reduce a Spell's Potency by the Withstand Attribute's rating. This means the Spell isn't being resisted, but rather it must overcome a threshold. If your player wishes to raise Withstand she needs only spend Willpower to raise the relevant Attribute.<br /> Do take into account the fact that Indomitable is a powerful tool nonetheless. It basically makes it so that your player needs only truly worry about Supernal attempts at tampering with her mind. Spirits and Goethia would be affected by Indomitable if they tried to mess with her brains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11807,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","user":"HTaiji","date":". 08-16-2016, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:21:16-07:00","id":951962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ifisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950999-2e-withstanding-merits?p=951745#post951745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit - For numbers comparison: average starting ventrue and mind mage vs average indomitable person. 2s for all relevant stats and the mage has a spell as a rote.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the value in this. Vampires and mages aren't supposed to be equals in how effective they are at things. Dominate needs to work for vampires, Mind needs to work for mage. The idea that something might be better or worse against one or the other is kind of silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2 mind, 2 rote mudra, 1 gnosis to best withstanding of 4 (resolve + indomitable). Required potency 5, primary factor raises it to 2. That's 3 more potency needed, or -6 dice. The mage is rolling a chance die, so success is unlikely. </div> </div> </div>Yep. The mage needs to do something to make their spell easier, like taking time for a second Yantra for more dice instead of trying to cast it in one turn. That's how Mage operates as a game. Doing some now and fast is much harder until you're very good at it, and at lower magical skills you're going to find you need to resort to less convenient methods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950999-2e-withstanding-merits?p=951869#post951869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indomitable does nothing to Withstand ratings</div> </div> </div> </div>While I appreciate an official response, and I get why this would be the case RAW, it does seem fairly... unsatisfying... that a Merit that's supposed to make supernatural mind control harder on a character doesn't work against mages because it doesn't interact with the right subsystem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:52:27-07:00","id":951990,"title":"","content":"The player is still more resistant to mind control powers, just not those of Mages.<br /> <br /> If you never plan on having them face off against a vampire or some other creature where it'd be useful I'd say refund it, otherwise don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:53:07-07:00","id":951991,"title":"","content":"Then a question we could ask might be &quot;How would you make it interact, and what are pros and cons of doing so from your perspective?&quot; <br /> Again, it's often enlightening to see things from different view point, and Dave has a pretty unique place to look from, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:49:26-07:00","id":952046,"title":"","content":"Regardless of official stance, I would grant +1 Withstand. I apply the same logic to other Merits, essentially granting half the normal bonus as a Withstand bonus. I find that this is balanced and doesn't diminish the value of certain Merits, which would be a form of power creep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}